# Model routing for {{ project_name }}

Three tiers, applied via `model:` frontmatter on commands and agents. Skills inherit the session model unless invoked through a tier-pinning slash shim.

| Surface | Tier | Model |
|---|---|---|
| session default | mid | `{{ model_mid }}` |
| `/security-review`, `security-auditor` agent | high | `{{ model_high }}` |
| `debugger` agent | high | `{{ model_high }}` |
| `/review`{% if enable_superpowers %}, `/review-with-superpowers`{% endif %} | mid | `{{ model_mid }}` |
| `code-reviewer`, `test-writer` agents | mid | `{{ model_mid }}` |
| `/commit`, `/techdebt` | low | `{{ model_low }}` |
{%- if enable_superpowers %}
| `/brainstorm` `/sp-plan` `/sp-debug` `/sp-skill` | high | `{{ model_high }}` |
| `/sp-tdd` `/sp-implement` `/sp-subagent` `/sp-worktree` | mid | `{{ model_mid }}` |
| `/sp-review-request` `/sp-review-receive` `/sp-finish` `/sp-verify` | mid | `{{ model_mid }}` |
| `{{ sp_prefix }}:*` skills (auto-fired) | inherits session | invoke via shim above for explicit tier |
{%- endif %}

## Why this mapping

- **High (Opus)**: deep reasoning, hypothesis formation, architectural judgment, security threat modeling. Cost is justified when the alternative is silent wrong-answer drift.
- **Mid (Sonnet)**: balanced execution. Following plans, writing tests, mechanical refactors, code review. Default for ad-hoc work.
- **Low (Haiku)**: deterministic mechanical tasks where structure dominates judgment. Conventional Commits, dead-code sweeps, format-only edits.

## 1M context window
{% if enable_1m_context %}
This project uses Claude Code's `[1m]` alias suffix on Opus/Sonnet tiers (e.g. `model_mid` = `{{ model_mid }}`). Per Claude Code docs (model-config#extended-context), `opus[1m]` and `sonnet[1m]` enable the 1M-token context window; Haiku has no 1M variant and the suffix is omitted automatically. Pricing: standard per-token rates beyond 200K — no premium. On Pro/Max subscriptions, Sonnet 1M may consume 'extra usage' quota.

To override at runtime without re-rendering the scaffold:
- Set `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT=1` in your env to drop 1M variants from the model picker.
- Or `/model sonnet` (without the `[1m]`) to switch the live session to the 200K alias.
{%- else %}
This project does **not** enable 1M context. To enable, re-render with `enable_1m_context=true` in `.copier-answers.yml`, or pin specific commands/agents to `{{ model_mid }}[1m]` / `{{ model_high }}[1m]` directly. Do not use `[1m]` on Haiku — it has no 1M variant.
{%- endif %}

## Aliases vs pinned IDs

The frontmatter values above use Claude Code **aliases** (`opus`, `sonnet`, `haiku`) which auto-resolve to the current stable release of each family. For reproducibility (e.g., long-running CI that must not drift across model bumps), replace each alias with a specific ID — `claude-opus-4-7`, `claude-sonnet-4-6`, `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` — either in `.copier-answers.yml` (re-run `copier update`) or directly in the `model:` line of the relevant `.claude/commands/*.md` / `.claude/agents/*.md` / `.claude/settings.json`.

## Changing routing in one place

The three values are derived from `model_routing` in `.copier-answers.yml`:
- `latest` → opus / sonnet / haiku (default)
- `sonnet-only` → sonnet across all three tiers
- `opus-heavy` → opus / opus / sonnet

Re-run `copier update` after editing.
